    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0210" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.607 South Seas/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in the Philippines</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sayre</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Manila</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-08T11:00:00+08:00">July 8, 1941—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. Reference the Department’s telegram No. 238, June 16, 5 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">8</hi>] p.m., the secretary to President has been
                    informed orally of contents. He gives assurance that nothing has been done or
                    will be done on the part of the Commonwealth Government and that Commonwealth
                    will keep in touch with influential organizations like the Chamber of Commerce
                    and will suggest to them the desirability of non-participation. Secretary added,
                    however, that the Commonwealth could scarcely see its way clear to prohibit
                    private firms in the Philippines if firms wished to exhibit at Tokyo.<anchor
                        n="76" xml:id="d208-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sayre</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d208-f1" n="76" xml:id="d208-f1-content">
                <p>Reports from consular officers in Batavia, Rangoon, Singapore, and Sydney
                    indicated a negative attitude on the part of the authorities as to participation
                    in the exposition.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
